&lt;p&gt;Sitting within our Engineering Enablement team, you won&#39;t just be fulfilling requests—you will own high-visibility data domains end-to-end. As our engineering and AI capabilities grow, the demand for clear, actionable intelligence has skyrocketed. We have around 190 KPIs across delivery, quality, investment, and AI adoption that need a true owner. This role is key in enabling and measuring the success of Anaplan’s internal AI initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We need someone who can take a vague question from leadership, figure out the underlying business problem, model the data, build the semantic layer, and deliver self-serve insights that actually make sense.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a &quot;data domain holder&quot; for 2-3 subject areas (e.g., executive scorecards, dependency health, investment mix, or DORA performance) from raw data to final stakeholder presentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and document semantic layers that outlast you, abstracting complex data from tools like Jira and GitHub into simple, self-serve reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Engineering team with development tasks and test data to ensure quality and completeness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior engineering leaders to translate ambiguous business questions into specific, defensible data answers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult and push back on requirements, identifying the most useful metrics and deciding what should and shouldn&#39;t be measured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine traditional metrics and AI telemetry to create meaningful measures of Anaplan&#39;s internal AI initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the dashboards tracking delivery, quality, dependency, investment, and AI adoption metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise the team on the evolving AI/BI tooling landscape (Rovo, Atlassian Intelligence, embedded AI), helping decide when to build versus when to consume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor junior analysts, championing data best practices so outputs remain clean and consistent as tool access broadens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building production BI in a fast-paced software or tech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python for the harder transforms and a strong working knowledge of development practices and tools (code repositories, build tools, scripting languages, agile development)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep SQL expertise and demonstrated comfort with dimensional modelling against warehouses with hundreds of tables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with enterprise BI tools such as Tableau, PowerBI, or eazyBI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of engineering intelligence, including DORA metrics, value-stream measurement, and CI/CD pipeline data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and consulting skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders, shape ambiguous requirements, and explain data limitations to executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy and the ability to own a domain end-to-end without needing a large support team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Atlassian data model (Jira, Confluence, Jira Align, JSM Assets).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a software development agency, SaaS environment, or a setting requiring you to manage multiple stakeholders and shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
